    {
      "kind": "section",
      "role": "model",
      "title": "Something else first: inversion",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "A time phrase, place phrase, object, or other sentence part can come first. The verb still stays in position 2, so the subject often comes after the verb. This switch is called "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "inversjon",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " (inversion)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "I dag drikker jeg te."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Today I drink tea."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Kaffe drikker jeg om morgenen."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Coffee, I drink in the morning."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Say "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "I dag kommer hun",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", not "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "I dag hun kommer",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "role": "model",
      "title": "Questions and sentence adverbs",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "In a yes/no question, the verb comes first. In most wh-questions, the question word comes first and the verb stays second: Når kommer du? If the question word is the subject, do not add another subject after the verb: Hvem kommer? Words such as ikke, aldri, ofte, kanskje, and bare usually sit after the finite verb in simple subject-first clauses."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Bor du her?"
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Do you live here?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Når kommer du?"
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "When are you coming?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Hva spiser hun?"
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "What is she eating?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Hvem kommer?"
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Who is coming?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Jeg drikker ikke kaffe."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "I do not drink coffee."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Jeg drikker ofte kaffe."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "I often drink coffee."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "I dag kommer jeg ikke."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Today I am not coming."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "I dag kommer ikke Per."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Today Per is not coming."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "At this level, learn the common safe pattern first: first field + verb + subject + sentence adverb + rest. With a fronted phrase, keep V2 and notice whether the subject is a pronoun or a noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "After a fronted phrase, pronoun subjects usually come before "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "ikke",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ": "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "I dag kommer jeg ikke",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ". Full-noun subjects often come after "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "ikke",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ": "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "I dag kommer ikke Per",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "."
            }
          ]
        },
